## Configuration

### config/asentric.yaml

- `chain` - Blockchain connection settings (chain ID, RPC endpoints)
- `source` - Event source (websocket recommended)
- `sink` - Alert destination (console for dev, webhook for production)
- `debug` - Enable debug logging

### config/registry.yaml

Add contracts to monitor:

```yaml
targets:
  - address: "0x..."
    name: "My Contract"
    abi_path: "abi/mycontract.json"
```

## Writing Custom Rules

Rules implement the `asentric.Rule` interface:

```go
package rules

import (
    "github.com/asentric/asentric/pkg/asentric"
    "github.com/asentric/asentric/pkg/utils"
)

type MyRule struct{}

func (r *MyRule) Name() string { 
    return "my-rule" 
}

func (r *MyRule) Severity() asentric.Severity { 
    return asentric.SeverityMedium 
}

func (r *MyRule) Evaluate(ctx asentric.Context) (*asentric.Alert, error) {
    for _, log := range ctx.Logs() {
        if log.Event.Name == "Transfer" {
            from := utils.GetFieldString(log.Event.Fields, "from")
            if utils.IsZeroAddress(from) {
                // This is a mint!
                return asentric.NewAlert(r.Name(), "Mint Detected!", r.Severity()), nil
            }
        }
    }
    return nil, nil
}
```

Register rules in `cmd/watcher/main.go`:

```go
engine.RegisterRule(&rules.MyRule{})
```

## Using Built-in Rules

The SDK provides reusable rules:

```go
import "github.com/asentric/asentric/pkg/rules"

// ERC20 Transfer detection (with mint/burn)
engine.RegisterRule(rules.NewERC20TransferRule(rules.ERC20TransferConfig{
    ContractAddress: "0x...",
    TokenSymbol:     "USDC",
    Decimals:        6,
}))

// Large transfer detection
engine.RegisterRule(rules.NewLargeTransferRule())

// Whale alert
engine.RegisterRule(rules.NewWhaleAlertRule())
```

## Utility Functions

```go
import "github.com/asentric/asentric/pkg/utils"

// Format token amounts
utils.FormatTokenAmount(wei, 6)      // "1000000" -> "1"

// Check for mint/burn
utils.IsZeroAddress(from)            // true = mint

// Truncate addresses for display
utils.TruncateAddress(addr)          // "0x1234...5678"

// Extract from event fields
utils.GetFieldString(fields, "from")
utils.GetFieldBigInt(fields, "value")
```

